  "id": "c6d582b1-2c5b-5b90-b7e5-4cda7b4e5d67",
  "slug": "caesar-dipping-oil-recipe-11983106",
  "name": "Caesar Dipping Oil",
  "recipe_type": "salad",
  "brief_description": "Inspired by the bold flavors of a classic Caesar salad, this savory dipping oil combines garlic, anchovies, lemon, and Parmigiano-Reggiano for an irresistibly rich and tangy appetizer. Serve with warm crusty bread for an impressive starter that\u2019s perfect for entertaining.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Smash garlic on a cutting board with the flat side of a chef\u2019s knife, and finely chop. Finely chop anchovy fillets and mash into garlic until a paste forms."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Pour both oils onto a large shallow platter or rimmed plate. Stir garlic-anchovy paste, lemon juice, salt, and pepper into the oil."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Stir together chives, parsley, lemon zest, and Parmigiano-Reggiano in a small bowl, and sprinkle evenly over oil mixture. Serve immediately with warm bread for dipping and scooping. Recipe developed by Marianne Williams"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": null,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 10,
